On Friday, July 03, 2015 15:31:59 spheniscine@gmail.com wrote:
> I also propose {la brivla}, to allow for coinages of names without having
> to define the brivla itself with a place structure. For example, {la
> dontivni} for YouTube.

It is, of course, possible for the same brivla to be used as a cmene and as a 
selbri. For example, {lo bercribe} means "a polar bear", but {la bercribe} 
means "Ursa Minor". (What to call Ursa Major I'm not sure. Ursa Minor's tail 
is at the North Pole.)

Also words and phrases can be entered in the Lojban Wiktionary.

